# qctl provision (instance)

Thin, command-oriented. Prefer shelling `qctl` over hand-writing YAML when unsure.
Full path: `qctl --help`.

## Layout (prefixed)

Under `provision/`:

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `common.yaml` | `qctl.environments`, `qctl.profiles`, `qctl.default-profile`, shared topology |
| `target-workstation.yaml` / `target-proxmox.yaml` | Hypervisor defaults for that target |
| `env-<name>.yaml` | Per-environment overlay |
| `profile-<name>.yaml` | Per-profile overrides |
| `.env.schema` / `.env.<env>` | Secret names + values for `!env` |

Select a profile with `-p` / `--profile` (default: `qctl.default-profile`).

## Grow the instance

| Goal | Command |
|------|---------|
| App (+ unit) | `qctl new app [name]` (`--engine rootless\|rootful`) |
| Unit under an app | `qctl new unit [app] [name]` |
| Environment | `qctl new env [name]` |
| Proxmox / extra profile | `qctl new profile [name]` (keep lab; **not** `init --force`) |
| Network / common package | `qctl new network\|common [name]` |
| Discover kinds | bare `qctl new` on a TTY |

## Validate

```bash
qctl init --check
qctl vm target-check          # host tools + provision for the profile
```

## Bindings / `!env`

- Secrets in YAML use `!env NAME` (optional `{ name, encoding }` for binary/multiline).
- Names are **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE** (`^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*(_[A-Z0-9]+)*$`).
- **Do not invent** secret names. Only add schema keys the user chose (or add-only via `qctl init --sync-env-from-yaml` / wizard).
- Values live in `provision/.env.<env>` for the profile’s env — not a fixed catalog of required keys.

## Happy path reminders

```text
qctl init . → qctl vm up → qctl new app demo --engine rootless → qctl sync → qctl vm up demo
Later: qctl new profile pve → qctl vm up --profile pve …
```
